# 91-modelerror-outcome-contract-and-stderr.patch (meta-soup 5bcf291c, 2026-07-31)
#
# The feat/cursor-detect-inline-model-errors + feat/cursor-model-error-bridge layers
# were DROPPED from the manifest (owner #987), but their fingerprints survive
# transitively via soup/cursor-model-error-fcm-bridge and the merged launcher/tests.
# That left the ModelErrorSendOutcome contract half-applied and the launcher stderr
# classification dropped. This backfills a COHERENT contract (the manifest note
# "the ModelErrorSendOutcome contract it needs is backfilled by soup-heals"):
#   - notificationTypes.ts: NotificationChannel.sendModelError -> (…, ctx?) =>
#     Promise<ModelErrorSendOutcome>.
#   - push / telegram / fcm channels: 3-arg signature returning the outcome
#     (nativeGate defer -> 'unavailable'; delivered -> 'delivered'; none -> 'failed').
#   - cursorAcpRemoteLauncher.ts: restore dropped @hapi/protocol + cursorModelErrorBridge
#     imports and the typed-stderr -> mapAcpStderrToFailure -> recordModelError path
#     (fixes "records modelError for typed rate_limit stderr" launcher test).
# The outcome return is currently ignored by notificationHub (dead-but-harmless);
# adopting it is less invasive than excising the leaked tests. Revisit if #987 lands.
